3. INTRODUCE STANDARD AND PRIORITY PICKUP

Add two pickup options to the booking experience.

Present them as two attractive cards with clear descriptions, expected collection times and transparent pricing.

These two options must be clearly different.

OPTION A: STANDARD PICKUP

Standard Pickup

“Get your package collected within 24 hours of your confirmed booking.”

Conditions:

* No additional standard pickup charge.
* Collection within 24 hours of confirmed booking.
* Pickup availability depends on the supported pickup area and operating conditions.
* Customer receives pickup confirmation.
* Customer receives updates when the pickup is assigned and completed.

The 24-hour period must begin when the booking is successfully confirmed, not when the customer merely opens the booking form.

Show the expected pickup deadline or collection window clearly.

Do not display an incorrect 2-hour collection promise anywhere.

OPTION B: PRIORITY PICKUP

Priority Pickup

“Need your package collected immediately? Choose Priority Pickup for instant collection.”

Conditions:

* Instant pickup handling.
* Additional priority pickup charge.
* Show the actual fee before confirmation.
* Show the expected collection time.
* Allow the customer to confirm or cancel before submitting.

Priority means immediate pickup handling and dispatch of an available pickup agent as soon as possible.

Do not falsely promise that a pickup agent will physically arrive instantly.

The system must check operational availability and show the realistic expected arrival time before the customer pays or confirms.

If instant pickup cannot be provided in the selected area or at that time, do not allow the customer to purchase the unavailable option.

Instead, explain that priority pickup is currently unavailable and show the next available pickup option.

IMPORTANT OPERATIONAL RULES

Do not invent pickup times or fees.

The system must use actual service availability, location, working hours, staffing and operational capacity.

Standard Pickup must use a 24-hour collection target after confirmation.

Priority Pickup must be offered as an instant-response service only where Swiftvero can actually provide it.

Allow the Operations & Admin team to configure:

* Standard pickup availability.
* Standard pickup target time, with 24 hours as the standard target.
* Priority pickup availability.
* Priority pickup fee.
* Priority pickup operating hours.
* Supported pickup areas.
* Pickup capacity.
* Available pickup staff.
* Blackout dates.
* Emergency service restrictions.
* Priority pickup restrictions.

Pickup charges must be separate from shipping charges.

Standard Pickup means there is no additional standard pickup charge. It does not mean that the shipping service itself is free.

The customer should always see the full applicable pickup charge before booking.

If a pickup is delayed beyond its confirmed collection window, record the delay and notify the customer with an updated expected collection time.

Do not silently change a confirmed pickup time.

